# Purpose

This document defines the authorization engineering standards for the hubIO platform.

Its purpose is to establish consistent principles for granting access to business capabilities while preserving organizational boundaries, business integrity, and long-term maintainability.

---

# Scope

This standard defines:

* Authorization philosophy
* Permission architecture
* Access boundaries
* Role responsibilities
* Authorization governance
* Permission evolution

It intentionally excludes authentication technologies, identity providers, access token implementation, and framework-specific authorization mechanisms, which are defined by their respective Engineering Standards.

---

# Constitutional Interpretation

This document extends the hubIO Engineering Constitution.

It applies constitutional engineering principles to authorization, ensuring business capabilities are accessed according to clearly defined responsibilities while preserving security and architectural consistency.

